To install ansible:
  1. sudo apt-add-repository ppa:ansible/ansible
	2. sudo apt update
	3. sudo apt install ansible
	4. sudo mkdir -p /etc/ansible
	5. sudo vi /etc/ansible/hosts
	          [servers]
            <worker_hostname> ansible_host=<worker_private_ip> (or)
            <worker_hostname> ansible_host=<worker_private_ip> ansible_user=ubuntu ansible_ssh_private_key_file=~/.ssh/<privatekeyfilename>
            [all:vars]
            ansible_python_interpreter=/usr/bin/python3



=================================================

From ansible-master: add the newly generated(using ssh-genkey) public key to worker node authorized key file in  .ssh/authorized_keys. 
dont give key name and paraphrase. Check the connectivity using: ssh <worker_private_ip>


If key name is provided then, perform any one for commands to work:
connectivity check ssh -i ~/.ssh/<privatekeyfilename> <worker_private_ip>
1.  sudo vi /etc/ansible/hosts on master
	[servers]        
<worker_hostname> ansible_host=<worker_private_ip> ansible_user=ubuntu ansible_ssh_private_key_file=~/.ssh/<privatekeyfilename>
2. While executing commands:
ansible all -a "free -m" --private-key=~/.ssh/<privatekeyfilename>
3. find the path for anisble.conf using ansible --version, update the file
[defaults]
inventory = ./hosts
private_key_file = ~/.ssh/<privatekeyfilename>
remote_user = ubuntu

To add ansible host entry as below:

sudo vi /etc/ansible/hosts

[testgroup]
kslave1 ansible_host=172.31.3.159
